# tgcli — Cursor agent rules

Canonical contract: `AGENTS.md`. Read `docs/MAP.md` and the tail of
`docs/DEVLOG.md` before substantial work. Scope lives in `docs/ISSUES.md`
and unvetted ideas in `docs/PROPOSALS.md`.

## Maintenance mode (ADR-0026)

- Do **not** add features or behavior changes unless the owner explicitly
  requests them. Then: ADR + scoped plan — never a new PLAN.md phase.
- Bug fix = reproducing test first, then the minimal fix.
- When unsure fix vs feature, ask the owner.

## TDD and verification

```
failing test → minimal code → green → docs → commit (if asked)
```

Before claiming done, run from the repo venv:

```bash
.venv/bin/pytest -q
.venv/bin/ruff check .
.venv/bin/ruff format --check .
.venv/bin/pyright
```

## Docs discipline

- Every session appends one entry to `docs/DEVLOG.md`.
- Architectural change → new ADR + index row in `docs/decisions/README.md`.
- Module add/move/remove → update `docs/MAP.md` in the same change.
- CLI flags / JSON / exit codes → update `docs/CONTRACT.md` in the same change.

## Hard constraints

- No daemons or background processes.
- stdout is contract data only; debug/progress → stderr.
- Never commit `.env`, `*.session`, audit logs, or `~/.local/state/tgcli/`.
- Branch: `claude/<topic>` or `codex/<topic>`. Do not push `main` unless
  the owner asks in the current session.

## Language

User conversation: Russian. Code, comments, docs, commits, CLI: English.

## How to task this agent (examples)

```
# Good — scoped, gated
Fix: tg api crashes on bool RPC result. Reproducing test first.

# Good — explicit feature gate
Implement MSG-001 albums only. ADR + plan before code.

# Bad — invites scope creep
Improve tgcli / add more commands / make it better.
```
